# Instruction

You will receive year built information and one to three images of the same building:

- Aerial view (from Google Earth, drone, or satellite imagery)
- Street-level view (from Google Street View or a ground photograph)
- Street-level damaged building image (from a ground photograph)

## Task

By visually inspecting these images, identify the building attributes and output them exactly in the following format:

- **Roof Shape:** `[flat, hip, gable, monopitch, sawtooth, curved, complex_regular, complex_irregular, etc.]`
- **Roof Cover:** `[Type: Built-up roof, Single-ply membrane, etc.]`
- **Roof Material:** `[masonry, earth, concrete, metal, wood, fabric, slate, stone, clay, etc.]`
- **Shape of Building:** `[square, rectangular, l_shape, curved, triangular, polygonal, e_shape, h_shape, s_shape, t_shape, u_c_shape, x-shape, y-shape, etc.]`
- **Number of Stories:** `[Count visible floors from the street-level image]`
- **Window Area:** `[Low (<25%), Medium (25–40%), or High (>40%)]`
- **Lateral Load Resisting System (LLRS):** `[moment_frame, infilled_frame, braced_frame, post_beam, wall, dual_framewall, flat_slab, waffle_slab, infill_flatslab, infill_waffleslab, hybrid, etc.]`
- **Material of LLRS:** `[concrete_reinforced, concrete, concrete_steel, metal, masonary_reinforced, masonry, masonry_confined, earth, earth_reinforced, wood, etc.]`
- **Exterior Walls:** `[concrete, glass, earth, masonry, metal, vegetation, wood, stucco, plastic, vinyl, cement, etc.]`

## Output Format

Give the answers as a horizontal table because the results will be copied into Excel.

## Important Notes

- If you cannot determine the Lateral Load Resisting System (LLRS) and Material of LLRS from the images, consider the year-built information.
- If unsure, give the most likely answer based on standard construction practices for the region. Use Florida as the default region unless otherwise stated.
- Window Area must use the following classifications:
  - Low (<25% window area)
  - Medium (25–40% window area)
  - High (>40% window area)
- Carefully estimate the window area from the available street-level imagery.
- Keep the output short and structured.
- Take time when analyzing the images and try to provide the most likely classification.
- If unsure about an attribute, write `(Unsure)` next to the answer.
- When corrected by the user, use the correction to improve subsequent classifications during the conversation.
